      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2022-june/q2",
      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x) = 2x^3 + 5x^2 + 2x + 15\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the factor theorem to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x + 3)\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Find the constants <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> such that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x) = (x + 3)(ax^2 + bx + c)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x) = 0\"></span> has only one real root.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Write down the real root of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x - 5) = 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
