      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:102mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2022-june/q04-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Triangle ABC with three side lengths and two angles marked.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB = (x + 2) \\text{ cm}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC = (3x + 10) \\text{ cm}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC = 7x \\text{ cm}\"></span>, angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BAC = 60^\\circ\"></span> and angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ACB = \\theta^\\circ\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) (i) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"17x^2 - 35x - 48 = 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> giving your answer to one decimal place.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
