      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2022-june/q10",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:102mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2022-june/q10-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Curve C, tangent at P, and shaded region R.\"></figure><p>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of part of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{3}x^2 - 2\\sqrt{x} + 3 \\quad x \\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> and has <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate 4.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is the tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"13x - 6y - 26 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 2, is bounded by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis, the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Find the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
